================================================================================
 v2redux — licensing
================================================================================

This repository contains code under public-domain terms, plus a test corpus of
third-party music that is NOT public domain. Read both sections.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. CODE  (everything except corpus/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All original work in this repository — the C++ port of the V2 engine, the
test and oracle harness, the build system, and the documentation — is dedicated
to the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal dedication.

    To the extent possible under law, the authors of this port have waived all
    copyright and related or neighboring rights to the original work in this
    repository. This work is published from Germany / Cyprus.

    CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

This port derives from the V2 synthesizer, written 2000–2008 by
Tammo "kb" Hinrichs, who placed his V2 code in the public domain. His original
dedication is preserved verbatim:

    -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    V2 code written 2000-2008 by Tammo "kb" Hinrichs

    I hereby place this code (as contained in this directory and the
    subdirectories "bin", "conv2m", "in_v2m", "libv2", "tinyplayer" and
    "tool") in the public domain.
    -----------------------------------------------------------------------

(Some original V2 source files additionally carried an "Artistic License 2.0"
header from their genthree lineage; the governing LICENSE.txt in the upstream
release is the public-domain dedication above. Original notices in ported
source files are preserved where present.)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 2. MUSIC CORPUS  (corpus/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The .v2m files under corpus/ are NOT covered by the public-domain dedication
above. They are musical compositions © their original authors (Farbrausch /
.theprodukkt), carved from freely-distributed demo releases and included here
solely as test vectors / ground-truth for the determinism and fidelity tests.

They are NOT relicensed and NO ownership is claimed over them. See
corpus/LICENSE and corpus/embedded/PROVENANCE.md for the per-song source and
provenance. Rights holders may request removal — see corpus/LICENSE.
